{"causes": ["The fragmentation of the Han Dynasty into the rival states of Cao Wei, Shu Han, and Eastern Wu necessitated strong military leadership.", "The strategic importance of Cao Wei's western borders, particularly the Guanzhong region, made it a constant target for Shu Han expansion.", "Zhuge Liang's ambitious Northern Expeditions aimed to restore the Han Dynasty by conquering Cao Wei's territories, requiring robust defensive responses."], "effects": ["Fei Yao's defensive actions contributed significantly to the preservation of Cao Wei's western territories against Shu Han incursions.", "He played a role in delaying Shu Han's expansion into the Guanzhong region, preventing a major shift in the Three Kingdoms balance of power.", "His military service exemplified the loyalty and capability of Cao Wei's generals, bolstering the state's military reputation."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "zhuge-liang", "sourceName": "Zhuge Liang", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "fei-yao", "targetName": "Fei Yao", "context": "Zhuge Liang's Northern Expeditions directly caused Fei Yao to be deployed in key defensive roles against Shu Han forces."}, {"sourceSlug": "fei-yao", "sourceName": "Fei Yao", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "battle-of-chencang", "targetName": "Battle of Chencang", "context": "Fei Yao participated in the Battle of Chencang in 229 CE, providing crucial reinforcements during the defense against Zhuge Liang."}, {"sourceSlug": "fei-yao", "sourceName": "Fei Yao", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "guanzhong-region-china", "targetName": "Guanzhong Region, China", "context": "Fei Yao's military career, particularly his defensive campaigns, occurred predominantly in the strategically vital Guanzhong region of China."}, {"sourceSlug": "cao-wei", "sourceName": "Cao Wei", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "fei-yao", "targetName": "Fei Yao", "context": "Fei Yao served as a loyal military general within the political and military structure of the state of Cao Wei."}, {"sourceSlug": "fei-yao", "sourceName": "Fei Yao", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "sima-yi", "targetName": "Sima Yi", "context": "Fei Yao collaborated with Sima Yi in 230 CE to counter Zhuge Liang's fifth Northern Expedition, defending the city of Shanggui."}], "places": [{"name": "Chencang, China", "role": "Major battle site"}, {"name": "Shanggui, China", "role": "Defended city"}, {"name": "Guanzhong, China", "role": "Region of operations"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Fei Yao", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "fei-yao"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q846999", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fei_Yao"], "tags": ["Military Leaders & Commanders", "conflict-and-resolution", "geopolitical-linkage", "temporal-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Fei Yao's consistent and successful defense of Cao Wei's western borders, particularly against Zhuge Liang's Northern Expeditions, was instrumental in preventing Shu Han expansion and maintaining the geopolitical balance of the Three Kingdoms period. His actions directly contributed to the stability of Cao Wei's heartland.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-05T07:19:29Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#28733010026", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Fei Yao was a military general of the state of Cao Wei during the Three Kingdoms period of China.", "newValue": "Fei Yao (died 230 CE) was a distinguished military general who served the state of Cao Wei during the tumultuous Three Kingdoms period of Chinese history. Operating primarily in the strategically vital western regions, Fei Yao's career was defined by his steadfast defense against the persistent Northern Expeditions launched by Zhuge Liang, the brilliant chancellor of rival state Shu Han. His contributions were crucial in safeguarding Cao Wei's Guanzhong heartland, particularly during pivotal sieges and campaigns that could have dramatically altered the balance of power in ancient China.

Fei Yao's early career saw him rise through the ranks, demonstrating acumen in both command and logistics. He gained prominence during the Battle of Chencang in 229 CE, where, alongside Hao Zhao, he played a critical role in repelling Zhuge Liang's fourth Northern Expedition. Though Hao Zhao is often credited with the primary defense, Fei Yao's command of reinforcements from Xi county provided crucial support, preventing the siege from collapsing Wei's defenses. Later, in 230 CE, he was dispatched by Emperor Cao Rui to defend Shanggui (modern Tianshui, Gansu province) during Zhuge Liang's fifth Northern Expedition, where he again faced off against the famed Shu Han strategist, collaborating with Sima Yi to counter Shu Han's advances.

Fei Yao's military service, though overshadowed by figures like Sima Yi or Zhang He, was instrumental in stabilizing Cao Wei's western flank during a period of intense pressure. His consistent performance in defensive campaigns against Shu Han's most formidable commander helped preserve Cao Wei's territorial integrity and allowed the state to consolidate its power elsewhere. His actions effectively stymied Shu Han's ambitions to reclaim the Central Plains, thereby contributing to the prolonged stalemate that characterized the middle phase of the Three Kingdoms era and ultimately paving the way for the Jin Dynasty's unification of China."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-05T07:19:29Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#28733010026", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Classical era: flourishing of philosophical inquiry, imperial expansion, and codification of la", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "150 CE"}, {"title": "Military conflicts and strategic necessities", "type": "Idea", "year": "150 CE"}], "newValue": ["The fragmentation of the Han Dynasty into the rival states of Cao Wei, Shu Han, and Eastern Wu necessitated strong military leadership.", "The strategic importance of Cao Wei's western borders, particularly the Guanzhong region, made it a constant target for Shu Han expansion.", "Zhuge Liang's ambitious Northern Expeditions aimed to restore the Han Dynasty by conquering Cao Wei's territories, requiring robust defensive responses."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-05T07:19:29Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#28733010026", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Determined military outcomes shaping geopolitical boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": ""}, {"title": "Contributed to enduring intellectual and institutional frameworks shaping subsequent civilizati", "type": "Movement", "year": "Classical"}], "newValue": ["Fei Yao's defensive actions contributed significantly to the preservation of Cao Wei's western territories against 